# Microsoft's VS Code server build the Microsoft-editor nightly runs (crates/puddle-app/e2e/microsoft-editor.mjs):
# `<release> <commit> <sha256>` of the linux-x64 web server tarball. The sha256 is the release server's own `sha256hash` of that
# exact release (https://update.code.visualstudio.com/api/versions/<release>/server-linux-x64-web/stable); the tarball comes from
# https://update.code.visualstudio.com/commit:<commit>/server-linux-x64-web/stable. The product itself installs the newest build;
# the nightly then replaces it with this one so the run does not change when Microsoft ships. A bump changes all three in one change.
